"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI am surprised by the freshness of the subject matter in Bernard's works, but left with disappointment at the too grandiose and forced conclusions.  \nA giant imagination with an anticlimactic ending\nCompared to the freshness of volume 1, the development of volume 2 leaves something to be desired.  \nThe mystery and tension carefully built up were solved too easily with the appearance of a too convenient setup.  \nThe narrative structure also repeats too much, which gives a sense of déjà vu.  "